      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## What is LLama2\n",
        "* Llama 2 is a Large Language Model (LLM) released by Meta AI in 2023. It is trained on huge amounts of text data and can understand and generate human-like language.It contain 70B parameters."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ZdbEpV2lXp34"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Why we need to fine tune Llama2\n",
        "* Free Google Colab offers a 15GB Graphics Card (Limited Resources --> Barely enough to store Llama 2–7b’s weights)\n",
        "\n",
        "* We also need to consider the overhead due to optimizer states, gradients, and forward activations\n",
        "\n",
        "* Full fine-tuning is not possible here: we need parameter-efficient fine-tuning (PEFT) techniques like LoRA or QLoRA."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "vNreVQt-X8w5"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Step -1\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1d_goMtGYgNU"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "* Load a llama-2-7b-chat-hf model (chat model)\n",
        "* Train it on the mlabonne/guanaco-llama2-1k (1,000 samples), which will produce our fine-tuned model Llama-2-7b-chat-finetune"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "pr9ePXGkYpsG"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from types import new_class\n",
        "# The llama model that you are using\n",
        "model_name = \"NousResearch/Llama-2-7b-chat-hf\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# the instruction dataset that you are using\n",
        "dataset_name = \"mlabonne/guanaco-llama2-1k\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fined Tune model name\n",
        "new_model = \"Llama-2-7b-chat-finetune\""
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "rG9hPY5AYeB9"
      },
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "new_model = \"/content/results\""
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zQx8yxKYYCR-"
      },
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### QloRa parameters"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "37Y8uVOwZ7Um"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Rank or Lora attention dimention\n",
        "Lora_r = 64\n",
        "# alpha parameter for lora scaling\n",
        "Lora_alpha = 16\n",
        "#Dropout\n",
        "Lora_dropout = 0.1"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mzA19D_NZ-YA"
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### BitsandBytes perameter (Use for quantization)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6sGVbyOtbNc8"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "use_4bit = True  #Load the pretrained model in 4-bit precision instead of full precision.\n",
        "\n",
        "# compute datatype for 4but model\n",
        "bnb_4bit_compute_dtype = 'float16' #The model is stored in 4-bit but computations still need higher precision. stores in 4 bit but do computation in 16 but full precision..\n",
        "\n",
        "# Quantization type\n",
        "bnb_4bit_quant_dtype = 'nf4' # Determines how weights are compressed into 4 bits.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "use_nested_quant = False\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "tpP6RN4daYaq"
      },
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Training arguments perameters"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jlcCBoBE69aH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Output directory where the model predictions and checkpoints will be stored\n",
        "output_dir = \"./results\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# number of training epochs\n",
        "num_training_epochs = 1\n",
        "\n",
        "# Enable fp16/bf16 training (set bf16 to True with an A100)\n",
        "fp16 = False\n",
        "bf16 = False\n",
        "\n",
        "# batch size per gpu for training\n",
        "per_device_train_batch_size = 1\n",
        "\n",
        "# batch size per gpu for testing or evaluating\n",
        "per_device_eval_batch_size =4\n",
        "\n",
        "# Number of update steps to accumulate the gradients for\n",
        "gradient_accumulation_steps = 4 # Update weights after every batch.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Enable gradient checkpointing\n",
        "gradient_checkpointing = True #The model stores fewer activations and recomputes them during backpropagation.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Maximum gradient normal (gradient clipping)\n",
        "max_grad_norm = 0.3     #Gradient clipping limits gradient size.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initial learning rate (AdamW optimizer)\n",
        "learning_rate = 2e-4   # How much weights change after each update.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Weight decay to apply to all layers except bias/LayerNorm weights\n",
        "weight_decay = 0.001  # Adds penalty for large weights. Reduce overfitting\n",
        "\n",
        "# Optimizer to use\n",
        "optim = \"paged_adamw_32bit\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Learning rate schedule\n",
        "lr_scheduler_type = \"cosine\" # find similarity and stable convergence\n",
        "\n",
        "# Number of training steps (overrides num_train_epochs)\n",
        "max_steps = -1 #Ignore max steps and use epochs instead.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Ratio of steps for a linear warmup (from 0 to learning rate)\n",
        "warmup_ratio = 0.03 #Slowly increase LR at beginning\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Group sequences into batches with same length\n",
        "\n",
        "# Saves memory and speeds up training considerably\n",
        "group_by_length = True\n",
        "\n",
        "# Save checkpoint every X updates steps\n",
        "save_steps = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "# Log every X updates steps\n",
        "logging_steps = 25\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "z6eEd6nM7A1Z"
      },
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### SFT (Supervised fine tuning)\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3MYJGZPA14Ik"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Maximum sequence length to use\n",
        "max_seq_length = None #Maximum number of tokens allowed as input.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Pack multiple short examples in the same input sequence to increase efficiency\n",
        "packing = False # Do not combine short examples\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load the entire model on the GPU 0\n",
        "device_map = {\"\": 0}  # put whole model on first gpu"
